I usually search with n11s (lazy), and repeat depending on how sure I am 
there's a door there. After a little while you get an uncanny knack for 
guessing the locations of secret doors. If I'm just scouring a room for 
any hidden doors I might think are there, I'll go around the walls (3 
spaces at a time) and only search 11 times each time around. If I reach 
the end of a corridor and there should be a door there, I may search 33 
times or more. If I'm REALLY lazy, I'll just kick the wall where I think 
a door is, or zap a force bolt.

You generally don't ever need to just press 's'. When you do n11s, 
you'll stop searching when you find something, and you were gonna search 
at least that many times if you didn't find anything anyway, right? 
It'll help keep an enemy from rounding the corner on you when you're 
tapping it too quickly.

